BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 750 Tm (TITLE: Kerala Agricultural University - Kuttanad Wetland Rice Acid Saline Soil Advisory) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 732 Tm (INSTITUTION: Kerala Agricultural University \(KAU\) Regional Agricultural Research Station Kumarakom) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 714 Tm (CROP: Paddy / Rice) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 696 Tm (TOPIC: Acid Saline \(Kari / Kayal\) Soils Nutrient Management) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 678 Tm (PUBLICATION_DATE: 2024) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 660 Tm (SOURCE_URL: https://kau.in/kuttanad-special-advisory) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 642 Tm (PAGE: 1) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 624 Tm () Tj 1 0 0 1 50 606 Tm (1. Acid Saline Kari Soil Amelioration) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 588 Tm (Symptoms: Heavy acidity with pH dropping below 4.5 and toxic ferrous/aluminum ion accumulation. Rice seedlings display rusty bronze speckling on lower leaves \(iron toxicity\).) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 570 Tm (Management & Remedy:) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 552 Tm (Leach fields thoroughly with fresh water before sowing. Apply burnt lime or dolomite @ 350-500 kg per acre in two splits. Maintain continuous saturation.) Tj 1 0 0 1 50 534 Tm (Citation: KAU Kuttanad Special Package of Practices 2024 \(Page 12\).) Tj ET
